        "id": 1402878
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-04T23:58:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`abi_gki_aarch64` is not an \"additional\" list, it is the default list. But you are right that it should be referred to as \n```\n  \"kmi_symbol_list\": \"android/abi_gki_aarch64\"\n```\n  \nand `define_common_kernels` should have entries like\n\n```\ndefine_common_kernels(target_configs \u003d {\n    \"kernel_aarch64\": {\n        \"kmi_symbol_list\": \"android/abi_gki_aarch64\",\n        \"additional_kmi_symbol_lists\": _aarch64_additional_kmi_symbol_lists,\n        \"abi_definition\": \"android/abi_gki_aarch64.xml\",\n    },\n```\n\nLeaving this aside, symbol lists are large as many modules use a quite large amount of common symbols. Just think of all the `str*` `mem*` etc. to begin with.\nAdditionally, symbol lists are not complementary, the qcom list should describe _all_ the symbols qcom modules need. That results naturally in overlaps among lists (intended) and long lists as well.",
      "parentUuid": "b5d66367_75020016",
      "revId": "33425f0a6dc1ab0b69af7e573680db736b870e3e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
